# =============================================================================
# Secrets and credentials — belt and braces
# =============================================================================
# Nothing matching these has ever existed in this repo: Kaggle credentials are
# read from ~/.kaggle/kaggle.json, outside the tree, and no other component
# holds one. These patterns exist so that stops being true by accident rather
# than by luck. Add to this block before adding a credential, never after.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!config/env.sovereign          # NOT a secret: offline + telemetry switches, §4.3
secrets.*
*credentials*
*.secret
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.ppk
kaggle.json
.kaggle/
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
.huggingface/
*token.json
*.token
service-account*.json
gha-creds-*.json

# =============================================================================
# Model weights and training output — bulk, and reproducible
# =============================================================================
# GitHub hard-blocks any single file over 100 MB and warns above 50 MB. models/
# alone is ~31 GB. All of this is regenerable from the refs that ARE tracked.
models/
workspace/
tools_ext/

# Third-party corpora fetched at build time.
# Reproducible from their Kaggle refs, so the refs are source and these are not.
data/external/

# Live fine-tuning stats: build-time output, regenerated by every run.
finetune/runs/

# Benchmark results are build-time output, regenerated by every run.
# Note the trailing /* rather than /. Git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a later negation can never re-include a file inside one —
# `!finetune/benchmarks/BASELINE.md` under `finetune/benchmarks/` silently does
# nothing. Excluding the contents instead is what makes the negation work.
finetune/benchmarks/*
# ...except the canonical baseline. It is the reference every adapter is judged
# against, so it is source, not build output.
!finetune/benchmarks/BASELINE.md
!finetune/benchmarks/BASELINE.json

# =============================================================================
# Local agent / editor tooling
# =============================================================================
# These hold absolute paths under the developer's home directory, so they leak
# a username and do not work on any other machine. .agents/skills/ also holds
# third-party skill packs that are not ours to redistribute.
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
.hermes/
.opencode/
skills-lock.json
.cursor/
.aider*
.continue/

